WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:06.920
Welcome to the Broadmeadow refurbishment&nbsp;
presentation. The following images allow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.560
us the chance to offer you a visual&nbsp;
representation of the proposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:17.920
refurbishment and decarbonization works&nbsp;
at Broadmeadow Sports Centre. Image one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.080
This image outlines the existing ground floor&nbsp;
plan showing the Sports Hall to the top left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.800
moving across to the gym before the Squash&nbsp;
Courts with the second gym area below the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.000
squash court. The annex building shows&nbsp;
the current change in toilet and office

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.960
areas. Image two. The existing first&nbsp;
floor plan shows the studios that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.680
used primarily for exercise&nbsp;
classes and indoor cycling

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:54.960
classes. Image Three. The blue areas noted on&nbsp;
the plan indicate the proposed gym extension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.320
achieved by removing some smaller areas of&nbsp;
internal walls and moving into the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:06.160
squash court area. These changes will enable&nbsp;
the targeted growth to the gym facilities. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.120
new downstairs exercise studio will be created&nbsp;
using court space from the Sports Hall that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.120
allow exercise program growth and enable the&nbsp;
opportunity for an accessible studio for our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:24.560
current and future users. Alongside female and&nbsp;
male toilets, changing and shower facilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.560
a village changing area will create accessible&nbsp;
changing areas for those needing supported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:36.400
access including family changing areas, private&nbsp;
showers with changing cubicles are also planned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.600
in this area. The reception entrance will be&nbsp;
relocated to the car park side of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:49.960
providing users with easier access&nbsp;
to the centre. Image four. The main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.760
exercise studio will extend across the newly&nbsp;
created downstairs studio enabling a greater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:02.240
studio capacity that will provide more space for&nbsp;
users to attend excise classes and activities.&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:07.240
The indoor cycling studio will be extended&nbsp;
slightly to increase the capacity in this area

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:16.840
too. Image five. Here is a visual representation&nbsp;
of the proposed new reception entrance which will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.360
be more conveniently located&nbsp;
for our users to access the

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:29.760
centre. Image six. The existing building&nbsp;
elevations are noted on this slide.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:43.120
Image seven. Proposed elevations are illustrated.&nbsp;
The west elevation shows the outside of the indoor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:49.080
cycling studio to the top right of the first&nbsp;
image. Cladding is proposed to reduce the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:56.080
thermal gains experienced in this area to help&nbsp;
maintain a more suitable exercise environment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.240
alongside improved air Handling Systems&nbsp;
planned internally will maintain more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:06.400
appropriate temperatures. The north&nbsp;
elevation shown in the bottom image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:12.720
offers a further indication of the proposed&nbsp;
new reception entrance of the facility. Our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:20.280
consultation runs until the 19th of January&nbsp;
2024 and we would welcome your feedback

